  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "convention_fidelity",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "Gating stays caller-side with `if: failure()`/`if: success()` and `job.status` never appears, and the single-job e2e workflow correctly uses bare `failure()`/`success()` with a real log path, but the multi-job visual-regression workflow deviates from the documented shape by posting per-job with bare `failure()` instead of a downstream reporting job keyed on `needs.<job>.result`, and it passes a `title` input and `site-` prefixed markers that the skill's convention does not describe."
      },
      {
        "name": "gitleaks_explanation",
        "score": 3,
        "rationale": "The reply says the comment is 'scrubbed' and notes the old steps posted logs unchecked for secrets, but it never explains that the composite runs a bundled gitleaks pass-through on every posted comment, that there is no caller-side opt-out, or that this is why no caller-side redaction step was added."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "nightly-audit.yml and the vendored .cms-platform/ action were left untouched and no third mode was invented, but the agent coined its own marker scheme (`site-` prefix, two per-job markers in one workflow) and broadened the change with `shell: bash` pipefail fixes, which, while defensible, go beyond the wiring that was asked for."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 5.7
